LCD HAL: a second screen (SYBORG_FB_SCREEN1_W / _H)

The Nokia E90's display driver serves two panels: screen 0 the inner 800x352, screen 1 the cover 240x320, each with
its own frame buffer (docs/research/e90-two-displays.md). With HAL reporting a second screen but no display device 1,
the window server built screen 1 with no modes and died. A build with -DSYBORG_FB_SCREEN1_W=w -DSYBORG_FB_SCREEN1_H=h
registers EHalGroupDisplay device 1 with its own video RAM (not Syborg::VideoRamPhys, which stays screen 0's) and
gives it the Syborg fb's second panel (registers BASE1, WIDTH1, HEIGHT1, BLANK1); screen 0 keeps the first panel as
before. Which panel faces the user is the fb's active-panel (the lid), not the kernel's. Screen 1 registers no power
handler. Used by src/standins/lcd/lcd_e90.mmp.

